{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1535739-hunter-aspects-how-to-use-them","id":1535739,"title":"Hunter Aspects: how to use them?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2024-05-16T10:41:58-07:00","id":1535739,"title":"Hunter Aspects: how to use them?","content":"As far as I could understand, when a pack is in Siskur-Dah they gain the benefits of the Hunter Aspect from the Auspice of the Uratha who presided over the ritual, is that right?<br /> <br /> Does it confer any kind of mechanical bonus? Or is something purely narrative?<br /> <br /> I'm also having trouble visualizing the Irraka's blissful in effect. Can anyone help me?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26311-ulbrecht","name":"Ulbrecht","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26311_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"33"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-16T11:08:07-07:00","id":1535740,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ulbrecht</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1535739-hunter-aspects-how-to-use-them#post1535739\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As far as I could understand, when a pack is in Siskur-Dah they gain the benefits of the Hunter Aspect from the Auspice of the Uratha who presided over the ritual, is that right?</div> </div> </div> </div>No. The <i>Siskur-Dah</i> gives you the benefits of the ritemaster's <i>tribal</i> Sacred Hunt benefit: The Blood Talon Hunt lets your pack perceive the prey's Renown. The Bone Shadow Hunt lets your pack touch and strike spirits in Twilight. The Hunt in Darkness lets your pack sense the state of the Gauntlet and whether your prey has tampered with the borders between realms. The Iron Master Hunt lets your pack choose the form their inflicted Lunacy takes. The Storm Lord Hunt lets your pack perceive whether someone is possessed, Urged, or Claimed. (All of this is on p. 310 in the Conditions appendix.)<br /> <br /> The Hunter's Aspect can be inflicted at will through actions exuding your predatory aura with a contested roll, and inflicts a temporary corresponding Condition. (This is on p. 98 under Hunter's Aspect.) The Cahalith's Aspect demoralizes the subject and impairs their Willpower. The Elodoth's Aspect impairs the subject's ability to coordinate with others in teamwork and combat. The Irraka's Aspect makes the subject complacent and distractible, impairing their Composure (and thus by extension their perception dice pool). The Ithaeur's Aspect clouds the mind and impairs the subject's Mental rolls in proportion to the weakness of the local Gauntlet, or impairs spirit subjects' rolls in general in proportion to the strength of the Gauntlet. The Rahu's Aspect makes the subject overconfident and makes it difficult for them to bring themselves to prepare for a confrontation with you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-16T11:10:22-07:00","id":1535741,"title":"","content":"Hunter's Aspect is a thing the werewolf can do to a subject at any time, imposing the Condition corresponding to the werewolf's auspice on the prey in question. It has no direct relation to the Sacred Hunt rite, whose variable benefits come from the ritemaster's tribe or lodge.<br /> <br /> The mechanical effects of the Hunter's Aspect and Siskur-Dah Conditions are described in the Tilts and Conditions Appendix.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-16T13:16:40-07:00","id":1535747,"title":"","content":"I see, I really mixed the two concepts... Thank you both for correcting me.<br /> <br /> But I'm more puzzled by the Blissful Aspect now. The only situation I can visualize it is someone being stalked and suddenly becoming distracted in their thoughts, not seeing the werewolf approach... And it makes it feel kin of limited in scope, I guess? Sorry if I couldn't be more clear, English is not my first language.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26311-ulbrecht","name":"Ulbrecht","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26311_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"33"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-16T14:03:52-07:00","id":1535750,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ulbrecht</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1535739-hunter-aspects-how-to-use-them?p=1535747#post1535747\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But I'm more puzzled by the Blissful Aspect now. The only situation I can visualize it is someone being stalked and suddenly becoming distracted in their thoughts, not seeing the werewolf approach... And it makes it feel kin of limited in scope, I guess? Sorry if I couldn't be more clear, English is not my first language.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Blissful aspect makes the target more susceptible to emotional manipulation and worsens their dice pools for perception and reaction to surprise, as well as reducing their Initiative. The target is made to inhabit a narrative context wherein they are the hapless prey who doesn't know they should be on their guard, just like the Dominant aspect puts the prey into the role of &quot;swaggering fool who doesn't realize they need to prepare themself against the deadly predator confronting them.&quot;<br /> <br /> The Hunter's Aspect is a tool for modeling how werewolves bend the world around them toward the hunt, and more specifically the type of hunt that they're predisposed to be good at.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}